","distance":0.6197,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Kevin Stefanski"}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"PIT","distance":0.3157,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"GB","distance":0.556,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"CLE","distance":0.5684,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"HOU","distance":0.5849,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"NYJ","distance":0.6098,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Jaguars are 7-2 through week 10 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 269 to 144. Both sides of the ball have been strong, with the offense 3rd in EPA per play and the defense 4th in EPA allowed. What sets them apart is the 3rd lowest pass rate and the 2nd highest eight man box rate in the league.","offense":"The Jaguars have one of the most efficient offenses in the league so far, ranking in the top eight in four of the five main efficiency measures. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Trevor Lawrence has run the passing game and leaned heavily on Parker Washington, who has drawn 26% of the targets.","defense":"The Jaguars have one of the best defenses in the league this season, ranking 5th or better in four of the five main efficiency measures. Its strongest area has been EPA allowed per rush, where it ranks 2nd, and its weakest has been sack rate, where it ranks 24th. Josh Hines-Allen has led the way with 2 sacks. In terms of scheme, they have the 2nd highest eight man box rate in the league.","special":"The Jaguars have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 90% of field goals, which is a little above average. Their salary cap was spread across positions in a fairly typical way.","players":"Trevor Lawrence has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 2,284 yards. Parker Washington has been the clear top target with 26% of the looks and 645 receiving yards. Bhayshul Tuten has handled most of the work in the backfield with 63% of the carries. On defense, Travon Walker leads the team with 3 sacks and Travis Hunter has picked off 3 passes.","coaching":"Liam Coen is calling the offense as head coach and Anthony Campanile is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2023 and 2022 Lions, both under Ben Johnson. Their defense looks most like the 2023 Steelers and the 2023 Packers.","trends":"The offense went from 14th in EPA per play in 2025 to 3rd so far this season, a big step forward. The defense moved from 3rd in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 4th so far this season, about where it was. The biggest change in approach was eight man box rate, which went from 5% to 14%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}